{
  "company_name": "SpendLens Manufacturing",
  "industry": "Machinery",
  "use_case": "Procurement spend intelligence and supplier performance analytics",
  "space_title": "SpendLens Manufacturing - Spend Intelligence 💰",
  "space_description": "**Subindustry:** Machinery\n\n**Use case:** Procurement Spend Intelligence & Supplier Performance\n\nSpendLens Manufacturing — direct- and indirect-spend analytics across supplier base and spend categories. Category Managers and Sourcing leads run quarterly category reviews and supplier scorecards; the CPO and CFO use it to drive realized savings, eliminate maverick spend, and de-risk concentration in the supplier portfolio.\n\n**Key KPIs**\n- Realized savings ($) — typical 3–5% of addressable spend, leaders 5–8%\n- Maverick spend (%) — leaders <5%, average 20–30%\n- On-time delivery (%) — supplier target ≥95%\n- Quality acceptance (%) — supplier target ≥98%\n- Contract compliance (%) — target ≥85%\n- PO cycle time (days) — efficiency lever, target <7 days\n- Supplier diversity spend (%) — ESG and corporate-goal metric\n- Cost avoidance ($) — value beyond hard savings\n\n**Data sources**\n- `procurement_transactions` — PO records with supplier, category, amount, delivery status, quality, maverick flag\n- `supplier_snapshots` — monthly supplier scorecards with OTD, quality, lead time, price variance, compliance\n- `spend_kpi_monthly` — monthly total spend, realized savings, maverick spend %, PO cycle time, diversity, cost avoidance",
  "schema_basename": "mach_spend_intel",
